   <text>
      <body>
         <div type="letter">
                <div type="address">
                    <ab>
                        <address>
                            <addrLine>
                                <name type="geo" key="G_FRA_PARI_11">26 Avenue Charles Floquet</name>
                            </addrLine>
                            <addrLine>
                                <name type="geo" key="G_FRA_PARI">Paris VII</name>
                            </addrLine>
                        </address>
                    </ab>
                </div> <div type="mainBody">
                    <opener>
                        <salute>Dear Miss Weaver:</salute>
                    </opener> <p>I am very sorry to get your letter with such <seg xml:id="seg1" type="note-anchor">bad news</seg>. It must have been a terrible time for you<supplied reason="omitted">.</supplied> I offer you my condolence. It is lamentable that such a sad event should be the beginning of the rest you need so much. I remember you were to have some there early in October. I can understand how dreary and lonely it must be for <seg xml:id="seg2" type="note-anchor">
                            <rs type="person" key="ID_MISSING">the other sister</rs>
                        </seg> and how trying for you<supplied reason="omitted">.</supplied> Please don’t fatigue yourself with any correspondence about <rs type="work" key="W_ULYSSES">my book</rs>
                        <supplied reason="omitted">.</supplied> I  hope sincerely that in some way or from your own patience and fortitude you will have some consolation and peace of mind.</p>      	<closer>
                        <salute>With kindest regards</salute>                	<salute>sincerely yours</salute>                          	<signed>
                            <name type="person" key="joyc82">James Joyce</name>
                        </signed> <dateline>
                            <date when="1923-01-13">13 January 1923</date>
                        </dateline>
                    </closer>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div type="notes">
                <note xml:id="note1" target="#seg1" type="commentary">Harriet Shaw Weaver’s aunt Emily died on 4 January 1923 in Frodsham. (Jane Lidderdale and Mary Nicholson, <name type="work">Dear Miss Weaver: Harriet Shaw Weaver 1876-1961</name> (New York: The Viking Press, 1970), 214.)</note>
                <note xml:id="note2" target="#seg2" type="commentary">Harriet Shaw Weaver’s unmarried aunts, Emily and “the other sister” Harriet Elizabeth Wright, had been living together in Frodsham.</note>
            </div>
      </body>
